# Secrets - never commit. A leaked CFBD key is the one catastrophic mistake (report 03 §11).
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# The raw data archive. Files are the source of truth, but they do not live in git:
# GitHub blocks files >100 MiB and Git LFS bills the repo OWNER for every fork's
# downloads (report 03 §5.2). The archive ships as GitHub Release assets instead.
archive/

# Model output. Regenerable from the archive by `make rankings`.
out/

# Static site build output (report 03 §7.1).
site/_build/

# Python environment and caches
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
*.egg-info/

# OS noise
.DS_Store

# Scratch outputs from multi-week fixture generation (regenerable; see Makefile)
.cache/

# School marks fetched for the share cards. Covered by `.cache/` above and named
# anyway, because THIS one is not merely regenerable, it is somebody else's
# property: the cards draw the marks for identification and this repository does
# not redistribute the files. What IS committed is data/logo-cache-manifest.json,
# the URL and sha256 of every byte drawn, which is how a reader verifies a card
# without us shipping a copy of anyone's logo.
.cache/logos/

# A local convenience symlink into another checkout of the same archive. `archive/`
# above does not match it: git stores a symlink as a file, so the trailing slash
# misses. Named explicitly so `git add -A` cannot pick up a machine-specific path.
archive
